# Compiled dictionary — 104 MB unpacked, ships via the model registry instead.
# Fetch from the GitHub release, NOT SourceForge (which returns 136 KB of HTML
# with a 200 status): 
#   https://github.com/r9y9/open_jtalk/releases/download/v1.11.1/open_jtalk_dic_utf_8-1.11.tar.gz
dic/

# CMake output, and the header upstream generates into its own source tree.
build/
upstream/src/mecab/src/config.h

# Model weights and exports — 493 MB, and the .pth is 355 MB of that. These are
# catalogue assets delivered through the model registry, not source. The export
# is reproducible from export_jsut.py; the SHA-256 in embedded_registry.json is
# what makes a delivered copy trustworthy.
jsut-vits/*.onnx
jsut-vits/*.pth

# Dictionary SOURCE csv (109 MB of the vendored tree). Not referenced by
# upstream/src/CMakeLists.txt — it builds only the analysis chain — and we ship
# the PRECOMPILED binary dictionary, so nothing here is needed to build or run.
# Re-fetch from the upstream zip if you ever need to compile a dictionary.
upstream/src/mecab-naist-jdic/
